+cowrie.mirage.respond
+=====================
+
+MIRAGE: the policy answered a command with ``respond``, and this is how that
+ended (only emitted when ``[mirage] responder_enabled`` is set, or the policy
+asked for an answer the decoy could not give).
+
+Attributes:
+
+    * `input`: the command line
+    * `outcome`: ``answered`` (the responder's answer was shown), ``fallback`` (no answer, nothing shown; the emulator's own command ran), ``cut`` (an answer stopped after lines of it were out) or ``cancelled`` (Ctrl-C)
+    * `reason`: why, for a fallback or a cut: the responder's own reason for aborting, ``ops:rejected``, ``timeout``, ``status:<code>``, ``error:<type>``, ``truncated``, ``malformed``, ``resync``, ``input_too_long``, ``journal_full``, ``tier:<tier>``, ``no_budget``
+    * `request_id`, `seq`: the same as the ``cowrie.policy.decision`` event of this command, and as the responder's own record
+    * `lines`: lines of output shown
+    * `first_ms`, `total_ms`: time until the first line, and until the end
+    * `rung`: what answered (``cache``, ``model``, ``replay``)
+    * `ops_applied`: state operations of the answer applied to the session
+    * `output_tokens`: tokens the answer cost
+    * `exit_code`: the exit status the command ended with
+
+cowrie.mirage.plant
+===================
+
+MIRAGE: the policy answered a command with ``plant_token``: operations that
+write a file holding a token, applied before the command ran.
+
+Attributes:
+
+    * `planted`: whether a file was written
+    * `paths`: the files written
+    * `reason`: why nothing was planted
+    * `decision_id`, `request_id`, `seq`: the decision this carried out
+
